<quest quest_id="13" category="training_quest" tag="Dredging Floor" published="False" valid="True">
	<title>Dredging Floor</title>
	<description>Learn more about how $[Skill.S.s_shipbuilding_NameSingular] and $[Resource.S.r_ship_fishing_trawler_NameSingular] works</description>
	<nodes>
		<node type="end_node" id="1" tag="">
			<actions>
				<action type="give_item_to_player" id="8" tag="An Add Item(s) to Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_Figurine Ship Fishing Trawler" quantity="1" inventory_type="Backpack" />
			</actions>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="2" tag="" optional_tasks="True">
			<instruction>Talk to any Spellmaster in a safe zone city</instruction>
			<journal_entry>If you&apos;ve wondered about what happens out there in the oceans surrounding the mainland of Agon, perhaps we can be of assistance. First off, ships come in many sizes and varieties. They can be fast and small, with limited firepower in the form of $[Resource.S.r_ship_cannon_item_NamePlural], or large and unwieldly like a $[Resource.S.r_ship_ship_of_the_line_NameSingular]. Anything as small as a $[Resource.R.r_raft_01_NameSingular] can get you out in the ocean, but some of the most useful ships like the $[Resource.S.r_ship_fishing_trawler_NameSingular] and the $[Resource.S.r_ship_sea_scraper_NameSingular] are much larger and can turn in a hefty profit when used correctly. You only need a single person to be at the helm to go sailing, but having company can prove life-saving out in the open sea.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
