		<node type="event_simple" id="3" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Try and get your feet wet first though before you aim for your own $[Resource.S.r_ship_ship_of_the_line_NameSingular]. Try your hand at sailing with this $[Resource.R.r_raft_01_NameSingular] first. Just point at some nearby sea and double-click the $[Resource.F.r_figurine_raft_01_NameSingular], climb aboard and press the Interact key at the helm.</journal_entry>
			<actions>
				<action type="give_item_to_player" id="0" tag="An Add Item(s) to Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_Figurine Raft_01" quantity="1" inventory_type="Backpack" />
			</actions>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="4" tag="" optional_tasks="False">
			<instruction>Gather the required materials in your bank</instruction>
			<journal_entry>Now that you&apos;ve gathered the materials talk to a spellmaster to tell you what you need to do.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="gather_items" id="17" value="1" tag="A Gather Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_Gold" quantity="3500" inventory_type="Bank">
					<task_instruction>Gather 3,500 $[Resource.G.r_gold_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
				<task type="gather_items" id="18" value="1" tag="A Gather Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_new Module Ship" quantity="6" inventory_type="Bank">
					<task_instruction>Gather 6 $[Resource.M.r_module_ship_NamePlural]</task_instruction>
				</task>
				<task type="gather_items" id="19" value="1" tag="A Gather Item(s) Task" resource_name="r_Ship Cannon Item" quantity="1" inventory_type="Bank">
					<task_instruction>Gather a $[Resource.S.r_ship_cannon_item_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="5" tag="">
			<instruction>Deploy the $[Resource.R.r_raft_01_NameSingular] by double-clicking the $[Resource.F.r_figurine_raft_01_NameSingular] and give it a spin</instruction>
			<journal_entry>While the raft isn&apos;t made for speed or firepower, it also cannot be crafted since it&apos;s not considered a real ship - and truth be told, it isn&apos;t one. To craft a ship, you mostly need $[Resource.G.r_gold_NameSingular] and some $[Resource.M.r_module_ship_NamePlural]. Most of the time, you&apos;ll also need one or more  $[Resource.S.r_ship_cannon_item_NamePlural]. Ships larger than a $[Resource.S.r_ship_coastal_runner_NameSingular] are mastery-level ships and require additional materials. If you&apos;re interested we&apos;d be happy to offer you a one-time chance to get a $[Resource.S.r_ship_fishing_trawler_NameSingular] which you can use for fishing at half the cost, without the need to skill-up right away.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="activate_item" id="36" value="1" tag="An Activate Item Task" resource_name="r_Figurine Raft_01" consume="False" />
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_merge" id="6" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Here&apos;s your fishing trawler! Now that you&apos;re all set, the High Seas are waiting! Get to a nearby shore, point at the horizon over water and double-click at the $[Resource.F.r_figurine_ship_fishing_trawler_NameSingular] to deploy it, swim aboard and use the helm. Before you know it, your box will be filled with fish ready to sell and you&apos;ll be better for it after the whole experience. Unless you get jumped at - don&apos;t forget you can use the spacebar to raise and lower your nets so that you don&apos;t lose everything.</journal_entry>
			<actions>
				<action type="take_item_from_player" id="4" tag="A Take Item(s) from Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_Gold" quantity="3500" inventory_type="Backpack" />
				<action type="take_item_from_player" id="5" tag="A Take Item(s) from Player's Inventory Action" resource_name="r_new Module Ship" quantity="6" inventory_type="Backpack" />
